sentences.text:
Therefore, as rightly pointed out https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis by the learned counsel for the second respondent/Insurance Company, for Sexagenarians, (i.e for the persons between 50-59),
while determining compensation towards 'Loss of Dependency' or 'Loss of Income due to Disability',
there is no question of adding future prospects, whereas, in the present case, the Tribunal, while determining compensation towards Loss of Dependency, committed an error in adding 10% towards Future Prospects, which is incorrect.
